# SemText sem-source — provenance chrome and the rendered/source toggle
# Direction A "Slate Console" (house reference-page look). One frame, a 2x2
# grid of four panels showing the wrapper's whole render contract: the two
# enhanced states (Rendered / Source), the class spelling without the reading
# tier (plain content), and the scripts-off state (identical plain flow). The
# drawing must make the PROVENANCE contract legible: a small chrome row
# (caption + segmented toggle) sits IN FLOW above the section it annotates —
# never floating over it — and the source state shows the authored markup in
# a fenced code card. Nothing generated ever obscures the content.
#
# MODE 1 — rendered (the element's `html` mode, the default):
#   visible: a small chrome row at the TOP of the panel — a short muted
#     small-caps caption bar on the left and a two-segment toggle on the
#     right (first segment active: thin violet border, violet text bar;
#     second segment plain) — then, beneath it in the same card, the section
#     content: a heading bar and a fact card with a bold statement bar and a
#     lighter conclusion bar, all fully legible.
#   must never: float or overlap the chrome on the content; dim or tint the
#     content; show a code fence in this panel.
#
# MODE 2 — source (the element's `source` mode):
#   visible: the SAME chrome row, but the SECOND toggle segment is now the
#     active one (violet), and the content is replaced by a fenced code card:
#     a dark code panel with a small "html" chip top-left and two tiny
#     control chips (copy, wrap) top-right, holding four-to-six indented
#     markup lines — nested tag/attribute bars suggesting HTML source —
#     entirely inside the card, never spilling past its border.
#   must never: render the fence lines outside or over the card edges; show
#     any rendered card content alongside the fence; put real characters in
#     the code lines.
#
# MODE 3 — class spelling without the reading tier:
#   visible: the same section content as MODE 1, identical position and
#     opacity, with NO chrome row and no fence — a plain block of content.
#   must never: add a toggle, caption, or fence in this panel.
#
# MODE 4 — scripts off:
#   visible: the same plain content block as MODE 3 — the degradation story:
#   identical reading, nothing hidden, nothing added.
#   must never: show generated chrome, or differ visually from MODE 3 beyond
#     trivial variation.
#
# All copy is abstract placeholder bars — strictly no letters, digits or
# words. Reference snapshots come from the snapshot-harness lane
# (`npm run snap:tag -- sem-source`, output into
# .tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-source/); the harness ran clean for
# this tag, so the best state captures are attached below as references.
schema: '0.4'
id: reference-sem-source
type: image
quality: high
service: gemini
model: gemini-2.5-flash-image

prompt:
  text: |
    Dark-mode UI mockup of a 2x2 grid of four reference-page panels on one
    wide 16:9 frame, flat technical illustration (screenshot-like, not 3D).
    Dark slate navy background (#0F172A) with a barely visible thin grid and
    a faint violet radial glow upper-left. Four equal dark slate cards
    (#1E293B) with thin slate hairline borders, squared corners, deep soft
    shadows; a tiny dim caption bar above each card. Generous gutters; all
    content inside each card stays fully inside its borders.

    Panel 1 (top-left) — RENDERED STATE. At the top of the card's content
    column, one slim chrome row: on the left a short muted small-caps caption
    bar; on the right a two-segment rectangular toggle — the FIRST segment
    active (thin violet #7C3AED hairline border, soft-violet low-opacity
    fill) and the second segment plain. Below the chrome row, clearly
    separated, the section content: one heading bar, then a wide fact card
    (slightly lighter slate, hairline border) containing a bold statement bar
    and a lighter conclusion bar. Everything crisp and legible.

    Panel 2 (top-right) — SOURCE STATE. The identical chrome row, but now the
    SECOND toggle segment is active (violet) and the first is plain. Below
    it, in place of the content, one fenced code card: a darker panel with a
    tiny chip top-left (thin border, one short bar standing for "html") and
    two tiny control chips top-right, holding five indented markup lines
    drawn as alternating tag bars and short attribute bars with clear nesting
    indent — all lines fully inside the card, no spill, no overlay.

    Panel 3 (bottom-left) — CLASS SPELLING. The same section content as
    panel 1 (heading bar + fact card with statement and conclusion bars) in
    the same position and opacity, with NO chrome row above it: the content
    starts at the top of the card.

    Panel 4 (bottom-right) — SCRIPTS OFF. The same plain content block as
    panel 3, visually identical: no chrome, no fence, nothing hidden.

    The chrome row (when present) is a slim in-flow strip above the content,
    never a floating bar, never overlapping, dimming or crossing the content
    beneath it. All copy everywhere is abstract placeholder bars — strictly
    no letters, digits, or words anywhere.
  negative: legible text, letters, numbers, digits, words, captions,
    typography, watermark, logo, light mode, white cards, rounded corners,
    3D, photorealism, faces, avatars, robot mascots, a floating chrome bar
    overlapping the content, a code fence spilling past its card border,
    rendered content and code fence shown together in one panel, generated
    chrome in the plain-content panels, any overlay or blur crossing content
  style: flat dark-mode product UI illustration, squared corners, hairline
    borders, slate and violet palette, four-panel state comparison grid

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1600
    height: 900
    aspect_ratio: '16:9'

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-source/sem-source-primary-render-1280.png
    role: reference
    description: rendered state — chrome row (caption + segmented toggle) in flow above a fact card
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-source/sem-source-primary-render-source-1280.png
    role: reference
    description: source state — Source segment active, fenced html code card with copy/wrap chips
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/sem-source/sem-source-class-form-render-1280.png
    role: reference
    description: class spelling without the reading tier — plain content, no chrome

requirements:
  subject: four panels of one disclosure wrapper — two enhanced states (rendered
    content, source fence) sharing one slim in-flow chrome row, and two plain
    states (class spelling, scripts off) with no chrome at all
  palette: slate navy background, slate panels, hairline borders, violet only
    on the active toggle segment and the faint corner glow
  composition: 2x2 equal panels; the chrome row leads its panel in flow and is
    never larger than the content; the fence stays inside its card
  do:
    - keep the chrome row a slim strip above the content, in flow
    - make the active toggle segment the only violet element per panel
    - render the fence as indented markup bars fully inside its code card
    - make panels 3 and 4 plain content, identical and un-chromed
  dont:
    - any legible text, digits, or logos
    - chrome floating over, dimming, or crossing the section it annotates
    - a fence that overflows or bleeds past its card border
    - generated chrome of any kind in the plain-content panels

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  criteria:
    chrome-in-flow:
      weight: 0.3
      description: 'The caption + segmented toggle row sits at the top of its
        panel as a slim in-flow strip above the section content, never
        floating over, dimming, or crossing it.'
      fail_signals:
        - chrome overlaps or tints the content beneath it
        - chrome rendered as a floating bar with content visible around it
        - chrome larger than the content block
    fence-contract:
      weight: 0.3
      description: 'The source panel shows one fenced code card (html chip,
        two control chips) holding indented markup bars entirely inside the
        card, with no rendered content beside it.'
      fail_signals:
        - fence lines spill past the card border
        - rendered card content appears alongside the fence
        - the code card missing its chips
    state-differentiation:
      weight: 0.2
      description: 'Panel 1 active segment first/violet, panel 2 active
        segment second/violet; panels 3 and 4 carry no chrome and match each
        other.'
      fail_signals:
        - both panels show the same segment active
        - violet on an inactive segment
        - chrome or fence present in panels 3 or 4
    legibility-and-palette:
      weight: 0.2
      description: 'All copy is abstract placeholder bars; slate navy palette
        with violet only on active segments; squared hairline cards; nothing
        illegible, truncated or occluded.'
      fail_signals:
        - any legible letters or digits
        - light mode or white cards
        - content bars truncated, occluded, or blurred
  reject_if:
    - chrome floats over or obscures the section it annotates
    - fence renders outside its card
    - any legible text anywhere
